<title>AUSTRALIA: CRICKET-SHEFFIELD SHIELD RESULT/STANDINGS.</title>
<headline>CRICKET-SHEFFIELD SHIELD RESULT/STANDINGS.</headline>
<dateline>PERTH 1996-12-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Result of a four-day Sheffield</p>
<p>Shield cricket match on Monday:</p>
<p>South Australia drew with South Australia - South Australia</p>
<p>258 (James Brayshaw 73, Darren Lehmann 52) and 381-7 (Jamie</p>
<p>Siddons 80, Greg Blewett 66, Jason Gillespie 58); Western</p>
<p>Australia 560 for eight declared (Justin Langer 274 not out,</p>
<p>Damien Martyn 104).</p>
<p>Standings (tabulate under played, won outright, won on first</p>
<p>innings, drawn, lost on first innings, lost outright, points):</p>
<p> Queensland		4   3   1   0   0   0   20</p>
<p> Tasmania		  4   1   1   0   1   1    8</p>
<p> Western Australia     3   1   1   1   0   1    8</p>
<p> New South Wales	 4   1   1   0   1   1    7.8</p>
<p> Victoria		  4   1   0   0   1   2    5.7</p>
<p> South Australia	 3   0   0   1   1   2    0</p>
<p>Note: New South Wales penalised 0.2 points for slow over</p>
<p>rate in an earlier match against Tasmania, Victoria penalised</p>
<p>0.3 points for slow over rate in another previous match against</p>
<p>New South Wales.</p>
</text>
